# Corresponding-source record for the components of the app image that need source, build material or
# relinking material: the two GPL kernel modules (morse.ko and dot11ah.ko), the hostapd programs and their
# statically linked libraries, and the release assets that carry the source. One row per piece of source or
# build material, with an exact revision or checksum. tests/test_source_offer.sh checks this file.
#
# This is a RECORD of what the binaries were built from and where the corresponding source is (the rows
# starting asset- name the release assets of version 1.0.0). It is not a legal conclusion. See SOURCE-OFFER.md for
# how the source is provided and what was checked.
#
# status:  recorded    pinned to an exact revision or checksum that can be re-fetched and checked
#          stored      the file itself is in this directory and its checksum is checked
#          described   a tool version or procedure recorded in words only; it cannot be checked by checksum (none at present)
#
# The rows with ids starting asset- name the corresponding-source release assets (provided as assets of the release v1.0.0); their
# checksums equal source-assets/ASSETS.psv.
#
# id | component | role | location | pinned_ref | sha256 | licence | status | notes
module-driver | Morse Micro driver (morse, dot11ah) | module source | https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse_driver.git | 4ce0a0272f8ac8e2fa58eea8ff08116e493399de | not-applicable (git commit id) | GPL-2.0-only | recorded | Tag mm8108-2.1.0. Built with the make command in source-offer/build-modules.sh (four CONFIG flags, KERNEL_SRC passed explicitly).
module-rate-control | mmrc-submodule (rate control), a git submodule of the driver | module source | ../mm_rate_control.git, relative to the driver repository's URL | 24f6c69dc9b78490b75cd181ad7013c1b3c3def6 | not-applicable (git commit id) | GPL-2.0-or-later OR a Morse Micro commercial licence (as that repository states in its LICENSING file and file headers) | recorded | Required for the build. The licence terms are taken from that repository's own statement and have not been legally assessed.
kernel-source | Linux kernel 6.18.58 (pristine source), linux-6.18.58.tar.xz, 154851680 bytes | build prerequisite | https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-6.18.58.tar.xz | 6.18.58 | 069b19f9032c4dac8149ae4b6520c35debca0f42a9f6d52ee55ba6ca9b818013 | GPL-2.0-only (with the kernel's syscall exception) | recorded | The checksum equals the single line kernel.org's sha256sums.asc lists for this file; the the listing's OpenPGP signature was checked on 2026-11-18 (good signature of the kernel.org autosigner key, which is not certified through a trust path) and the tarball's detached signature was not fetched. The modules are built against this tree after the patches and configuration below are applied.
os-source | Home Assistant Operating System 18.4 (patches, kernel configuration fragments, toolchain selection), GitHub archive 18.4.tar.gz, 342411 bytes, SHA-256 7d9f23cfe96e88a2d3aeb9cde33cb0f7005c3a343a11db05b54e231c886b85cd | build prerequisite | https://github.com/home-assistant/operating-system.git | 4a7dab478abc8f959c0fc2c24876d08282a3c060 | not-applicable (git commit id) | various; see that repository | recorded | Tag 18.4. The commit id is read from the downloaded archive's pax header (git get-tar-commit-id); the archive checksum identifies that one download only, because GitHub archive hashes are not guaranteed stable. green_defconfig at this commit selects kernel 6.18.58, the configuration fragments and the patch set listed in the rows below.
