kernel-config-final | the final kernel configuration the modules were built against | build prerequisite | source-offer/kernel-6.18.58-haos.config in this directory | not-applicable (stored file) | 796504d949af46211a2335632054527a761c39a67d371f78294a5a8d925e48ab | GPL-2.0-only | stored | The .config of the locally prepared 6.18.58 kernel tree after olddefconfig with the GCC 13.4.0 toolchain below (CONFIG_MODVERSIONS not set). It differs from the configuration derived from the official image (kernel-config-derived, SHA-256 a4426c779010b70d480504acc70948c3363960d2d0a5fe1fba1c32cd3b1aac4c) in exactly one line, CONFIG_CC_VERSION_TEXT: this tree has the Buildroot commit d2b75e05 text, the official one has -g30c038aa. Replacing that line gives the derived file byte for byte (checked by hash).
kernel-config-derived | the kernel configuration derived from the official 18.4 image | build prerequisite | the decompressed config.gz embedded in the kernel image of haos_green-18.4.img.xz (SHA-256 b5d9a4869a9c70a9d87946f8ba90c72b0a42b393404fa8bf82e161452b8c6aba); the update bundle haos_green-18.4.raucb (SHA-256 8e7189352061686fb9c54bacdd6fe8fa700a50ec5af5630df1cf0af39ff25a3f) carries the same kernel image | not-applicable (derived from a download, not stored here) | a4426c779010b70d480504acc70948c3363960d2d0a5fe1fba1c32cd3b1aac4c | GPL-2.0-only | recorded | 276698 bytes, 10853 lines. Installed as .config before olddefconfig. As published on the GitHub release; the signature chain of that release was not verified.
toolchain-source | Buildroot (Home Assistant fork), used to build the cross toolchain | build prerequisite | https://github.com/home-assistant/buildroot.git | d2b75e0548bf1f0c56d17cac44d5fe9a0e17e60a | not-applicable (git commit id) | GPL-2.0-or-later and the licences of the packages it builds | recorded | The commit the Operating System 18.3 tag referenced; it was reused for the 6.18.58 build and is NOT the commit that built the official 18.4 image (the 18.4 kernel banner names Buildroot -g30c038aa; that Buildroot commit was not fetched). Only its toolchain target was built (make toolchain), targeting aarch64-buildroot-linux-gnu with the Operating System external tree.
toolchain-gcc | GCC 13.4.0 (Buildroot -gd2b75e05) | build prerequisite | built by toolchain-source | 13.4.0 | not-applicable (built from the package's own pinned source) | GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception | recorded | Compiler used for the 6.18.58 tree and the modules. The 18.4 kernel banner reports GCC 13.4.0 with Buildroot -g30c038aa: the version number is the same, byte-identical output is not established.
toolchain-binutils | GNU Binutils 2.43.1 | build prerequisite | built by toolchain-source | 2.43.1 | not-applicable (built from the package's own pinned source) | GPL-3.0-or-later | recorded | Linker used for the modules. The 18.4 kernel banner reports the same version (2.43.1).
build-script | the module build and comparison script | build script | source-offer/build-modules.sh in this directory | not-applicable (stored file) | 3e9100f7145bd01c2c4652ad82502fc5b162867271cecddcefa08fe1ed1235af | Apache-2.0 (the product's own build script; see LICENSE) | stored | Pins the driver and submodule commits, records and prints the 18.4 build inputs, runs the make command (path-independent by default), and compares the result with MANIFEST.sha256. With DRIVER_FROM_ARCHIVE=1 the driver directory may be an extraction of the driver source release asset (no git history needed); the modules rebuilt that way on 2026-11-18 gave MATCH for both files.
toolchain-config | the Buildroot configuration the toolchain was built with (path-normalised) | build prerequisite | source-offer/buildroot-toolchain.config in this directory | not-applicable (stored file) | 79845972fd178b1b4e6cca58eb21d41be83688adc6ac5eea2a1357ada1b2a177 | not-applicable | stored | The configuration of the toolchain build with the build machine's absolute paths replaced by placeholders and its date header lines removed (the unnormalised file's own checksum is c98c1fff242b16ffb5745008b8e54572dbfca5b1c19d5ba01e6edd43ebef3969 and is not stored). It is NOT identical to what green_defconfig regenerates: it additionally builds static libraries (BR2_SHARED_STATIC_LIBS instead of shared-only), without PIE and RELRO-full; a regeneration from green_defconfig differs in those lines and in the package options that depend on them. Those are the differences found; a full end-to-end rebuild of the toolchain from this file was not done.
kernel-prep-compiler | cross compiler used for the 6.18.58 kernel build (vmlinux, modules, Module.symvers) | build prerequisite | the toolchain of the toolchain-source row (GCC 13.4.0, binutils 2.43.1, aarch64-buildroot-linux-gnu) | Buildroot commit d2b75e0548bf1f0c56d17cac44d5fe9a0e17e60a (GCC 13.4.0, binutils 2.43.1) | not-applicable | GPL-3.0-or-later | recorded | The whole 6.18.58 tree was built with this one toolchain (unlike the 6.18.52 tree, which was first built with another compiler); the kernel's host tools (modpost, fixdep) were built with the build machine's own compiler, whose version is not recorded for this build. The in-tree cfg80211, mac80211 and libarc4 modules have different GNU build-ids from the published 18.4 host modules (cfg80211 bee86120 against 834e2f76, mac80211 3bbbb207 against 488f6476, libarc4 7d420f4f against 5442ed19), so the tree is not byte-identical to the build that made the image; the likely contributors (the toolchain commit, build path, user and time strings) were not tested.
kernel-prep-sequence | the script that prepared the 6.18.58 kernel tree | build script | source-offer/kernel-prep.sh in this directory (also the release asset kernel-prep.sh) | not-applicable (stored file) | 2e4503a7b41242505ce245124f9edea8dbbca6758a8b5f5ab885412062a561e3 | Apache-2.0 (the product's own build script; see LICENSE) | stored | The script was run on 2026-10-28 (exit 0, nine patches). Only comments and the text of one error message differ from the script that was run. Its steps: 1 check the tarball against the published checksum and unpack it; 2 apply the nine patches (git apply, in the order of the kernel-patch rows); 3 install the derived configuration as .config and run olddefconfig with the GCC 13.4.0 toolchain; 4 check that the kernel release is 6.18.58-haos and that olddefconfig changed nothing but the compiler text lines; 5 one full build (make vmlinux modules, all processors, about 2 hours 20 minutes), producing Module.symvers; 6 build the two modules with source-offer/build-modules.sh (PATH_INDEPENDENT=1 is the default).
hostap-source | Morse Micro hostap fork, tag mm8108-2.1.0 (hostapd_s1g, hostapd_cli_s1g and the configuration template) | executable source (not the kernel modules) | https://github.com/MorseMicro/hostap.git (also the release asset hostap-source-2.1.0.tar.gz) | e7309b438eaec4b82f2db29e8ef7beaca3ca52c6 | not-applicable (git commit id) | BSD-3-Clause AND ISC (BSD-3-Clause at repository level, one compiled file under ISC; see provenance.psv) | recorded | The same release as the driver and firmware. Replaces tag 1.17.9 (commit beed5f8c827fa4b6dc77ec9d467c84cdee50fdda), which the add-on used before together with a separate helper program; this release talks to the driver over nl80211 vendor commands and needs no helper. Built from the tag's own hostapd/defconfig, which enables CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MORSE and CONFIG_MORSE_5GHZ_MAPPED, with DPP, DPP2, DPP3 and OWE switched off, and with -Wno-error=unused-variable because the tag fails its own -Werror build otherwise (src/ap/ap_config.c:849). The toolchain is unchanged (toolchain-source, toolchain-config). The executables are outside the module record; this row only names the source.
hostap-build-script | the hostapd build script | build script | source-offer/build-hostapd.sh in this directory | not-applicable (stored file) | 5ee4e4f08785abb437ba7a4f5f110688e9387c1c222a1a0973f03390d858566f | Apache-2.0 (the product's own build script; see LICENSE) | stored | Pins the hostap commit and the OpenSSL 3.5.9 tarball checksum and takes the toolchain location from the environment. It builds OpenSSL (static, install prefix /usr/local, openssldir /usr/local/ssl, into a staging directory), applies the configuration of the hostap-source row with path-neutral flags (file-prefix-map for the source, toolchain, sysroot and OpenSSL paths, no build id, a fixed source date, locale and time zone, deterministic archives), strips both executables with the toolchain's own strip and writes the unstripped builds to a separate debug directory. It compares the stripped executables with MANIFEST.sha256 when that file is present. Run three times from different directories with different time zone, locale, user name and file times, once from a fresh clone of the tag with a freshly downloaded OpenSSL tarball and a copy of the toolchain at another path: byte-identical executables each time. The toolchain was reused as already built, not rebuilt. The script requires a clean source tree and prints the compiler version. With HOSTAP_FROM_ARCHIVE=1 the hostap directory may be an extraction of the release asset hostap-source-2.1.0.tar.gz (no git history needed); both executables matched MANIFEST.sha256 when built that way on 2026-11-18. Not run on a device.
static-lib-openssl | OpenSSL 3.5.9 (statically linked into hostapd_s1g) | static library source (executables, not the kernel modules) | https://github.com/openssl/openssl (release 3.5.9 tarball) | tag openssl-3.5.9 | 603f5602e2eef00d77fbd429d34dcd5822bb301757a1bc9cdb24c670f1eb859a | Apache-2.0 | recorded | Added 2026-10-28 for completeness; the checksum is that of the release tarball as provenance.psv records it. The executables are outside the module record; this row only names the source. Rebuilt by source-offer/build-hostapd.sh from this tarball with the configure options recorded in provenance.psv (embedded:openssl) and neutral install locations.
static-lib-glibc | GNU C Library 2.41-161-g5dd252cf (statically linked into hostapd_s1g and hostapd_cli_s1g) | static library source (executables, not the kernel modules) | https://gitlab.com/gnutools/glibc.git | 5dd252cf1d113644b3679f5a158e9ef20217865e | not-applicable (git commit id) | LGPL-2.1-or-later (COPYING.LIB read at the pinned commit) | recorded | Version and commit as provenance.psv records them. The source is the release asset glibc-2.41-5dd252cf.tar.gz (the archive the Buildroot toolchain build fetched); the relink material is the release asset hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz. COPYING.LIB and LICENSES were read at the pinned commit.
static-lib-libnl | libnl 3.11.0 (libnl-3 and libnl-genl-3, statically linked into hostapd_s1g) | static library source (executables, not the kernel modules) | https://github.com/thom311/libnl/releases/download/libnl3_11_0/libnl-3.11.0.tar.gz | 3.11.0 | 2a56e1edefa3e68a7c00879496736fdbf62fc94ed3232c0baba127ecfa76874d | LGPL-2.1-only | recorded | Tarball checksum as the toolchain build's Buildroot package pins it (recorded in provenance.psv). The source is the release asset libnl-3.11.0.tar.gz (the same bytes); the relink material is the release asset hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz.
static-lib-libgcc | GCC 13.4.0 runtime library (libgcc, statically linked into the executables) | static library source (executables, not the kernel modules) | https://github.com/home-assistant/buildroot.git (the Buildroot GCC package builds it) | d2b75e0548bf1f0c56d17cac44d5fe9a0e17e60a | not-applicable (git commit id) | GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception (COPYING3 and COPYING.RUNTIME of GCC 13.4.0 read) | recorded | The same Buildroot commit as toolchain-source. The runtime library exception allows distribution of the combined executables without the GCC source; whether this build qualifies was not verified, so no GCC 13.4.0 source is in the release assets (the Alpine gcc source for the base image libgcc and libstdc++ is).
